// Per melee class: how it plays the cut rows of `actions.ron`. The body has
// one set of cut clips, so a class does not own a moveset yet: it scales the
// Light, Followup and Heavy rows, and the same clips play slower or faster
// while the same sweep reaches further. A Blade is the rows exactly as
// `actions.ron` has them (every factor one), which is what a sheet's boxes
// are written against; a box still changes the row first and the class
// scales what is left.
//
// blade_reach_m: metres the baked sweep reaches from the hand, used only to
// say a reach in metres.
// reach: a factor on how far along and beyond the baked blade the sweep's
// points lie.
// light is applied to Light and Followup, heavy to Heavy. time scales
// contact_start, contact_end, duration and dodge_cancel together; damage,
// posture, stamina and travel scale the row's own figures.
// swing_posture: the share of incoming posture damage the holder takes while
// one of its own cuts is under way (one is no protection).
//
// caught: what a cut made with a melee weapon (a light, a follow up, a heavy,
// an ability's strike) multiplies on a bearer whose hand holds a gun and whose
// guard does not meet it: a gun is no guard. Posture and damage are factors
// on the cut's own, stagger on the length of the stagger when that cut is the
// one that breaks the bearer; a bolt, or a cut on a melee bearer, never reads
// it.
//
// The guard is the aim button held with a melee weapon in hand, a Ready
// actor's state that any other action ends.
// parry_rest: seconds a guard must have been down before raising it can
// parry again, so a hammered button is not a standing parry.
// guard_regen: the share of stamina regeneration kept while the guard is up.
// guard, per class: share is the part of a hit's damage a guard takes off;
// arc the half angle, in degrees either side of the facing, a hit must come
// from to meet it; stamina what a point of damage taken off costs; posture
// the part of a hit's posture damage that still lands through it; parry the
// seconds after it is raised in which a hit is parried; riposte the posture
// damage a parried cut gives its attacker.
(
    version: 4,
    blade_reach_m: 1.7,
    parry_rest: 0.5,
    guard_regen: 0.35,
    caught: (posture: 1.6, damage: 1.0, stagger: 1.5),
    classes: {
        Blade: (
            reach: 1.0,
            light: (time: 1.0, damage: 1.0, posture: 1.0, stamina: 1.0, travel: 1.0),
            heavy: (time: 1.0, damage: 1.0, posture: 1.0, stamina: 1.0, travel: 1.0),
            swing_posture: 1.0,
            guard: (share: 0.60, arc: 70, stamina: 1.40, posture: 0.40, parry: 0.20, riposte: 70),
        ),
        Greatblade: (
            reach: 1.3,
            light: (time: 1.75, damage: 1.65, posture: 1.70, stamina: 1.65, travel: 1.0),
            heavy: (time: 1.35, damage: 1.65, posture: 1.65, stamina: 1.50, travel: 1.0),
            swing_posture: 0.3,
            guard: (share: 0.80, arc: 80, stamina: 0.70, posture: 0.20, parry: 0.10, riposte: 90),
        ),
        Glaive: (
            reach: 1.75,
            light: (time: 1.35, damage: 1.15, posture: 1.00, stamina: 1.20, travel: 1.2),
            heavy: (time: 1.20, damage: 1.10, posture: 1.00, stamina: 1.20, travel: 1.4),
            swing_posture: 1.0,
            guard: (share: 0.50, arc: 60, stamina: 1.70, posture: 0.50, parry: 0.14, riposte: 60),
        ),
    },
)
